{
  "requirement": "`ValidationCache::new()` creates an empty cache for running criteria without\nan agent.\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl ValidationCache {\n    pub fn new() -> Self;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.validation-cache.new` has one obligation: `ValidationCache::new()` returns an empty cache with no agent, for running criteria without an agent.\n\n- **Unit test:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs#mod[tests]/fn[new_cache_starts_without_files_or_agent]` calls `ValidationCache::new()`. It asserts that the `outlines` map is empty and that `agent` is `None`. Together these check both parts of the requirement, an empty cache and no agent.\n- **Contract test:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_clones_share_the_first_successful_outline_for_each_path]` also carries a `{test}` reference to `requirements.sdk.validation-cache.new`. It builds a fresh cache with `new()` and shows the cache starts without a cached outline. The first `OutlineContent::from_path` call on a missing file returns an error. After the file is written, the first call returns a snapshot of the written content, so nothing was pre-populated.\n- **Unasserted field:** `ValidationCache` also has a `sources` field. The unit test doesn't assert it is `None`. `new()` takes no arguments and is `Self::default()`, so it has no source to attach. The requirement's text doesn't mention `sources`, so I don't count this as a gap.\n\nI found no unacknowledged gaps.",
